Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The earlier design’s core idea was sound, but its progress argument was not:
// opening `<<` and closing `>>` can add delimiter tokens in a single charged
// step, so a one-token-per-step growth bound is too weak. This revision keeps
// the same conservative, parser-guided behavior while switching to a growth
// invariant that charges at most two generated tokens per step. That matches the
// helper effects we rely on: unconstrained sampling and constrained appends add
// at most one token, while opening or closing a span may add the two-character
// delimiter token sequence represented as one token each in the token stream,
// and the proof only needs the coarse bound that each charged step increases
// `generated` by no more than 2.
//
// Outside constrained mode, the strategy looks at the model’s current logits and
// opens `<<` only when that token is already competitive; otherwise it samples
// unconstrained text. Inside constrained mode, it closes immediately once the
// arithmetic prefix is complete; otherwise it tries the current argmax only if
// that token is parser-valid and not EOS, and falls back to `ConstrainedStep`
// when the argmax is unsuitable. This preserves the creative behavior of using
// model preference when safe, while ensuring constrained content remains parser-
// valid and that completed arithmetic spans are terminated eagerly with `>>`.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
// - Outside/non-opening and outside/EOS branches keep `insideConstrainedOut`
//   false, so the implication is vacuous. The outside/open branch uses
//   `OpenConstrainedSpan`, which returns an active empty constrained prefix;
//   `parser.IsValidPrefix([])` holds by precondition, so validity is preserved.
// - Inside/complete uses `CloseConstrainedSpan`, after which
//   `insideConstrainedOut` is false, making the implication vacuous.
// - Inside/incomplete with raw sampling: if sampled token is EOS we break
//   without changing constrained state, so the invariant still holds at loop
//   exit. If the sampled token is parser-valid, `AppendConstrainedToken` extends
//   the constrained prefix by a valid next token; if sampled token is invalid we
//   instead append `best`, whose validity was established by
//   `IsTokenValidNext`. Inside/incomplete with `ConstrainedStep` is analogous:
//   EOS breaks with unchanged state; otherwise the helper returns a valid next
//   token, and `AppendConstrainedToken` preserves validity.
//
// suffix:
// - Outside/non-opening and outside/EOS keep `insideConstrainedOut` false, so
//   the suffix implication is vacuous. Outside/open sets the active constrained
//   content to empty; the length-0 suffix of any sequence is `[]`, so the suffix
//   property holds immediately after opening.
// - Inside/complete closes the span, making `insideConstrainedOut` false and the
//   implication vacuous.
// - Inside/incomplete EOS breaks without mutating `generated` or
//   `currentConstrainedOut`, so the previous suffix relation remains true. In
//   every constrained append branch, `AppendConstrainedToken` appends the same
//   token to both `generated` and the active constrained prefix, so the suffix
//   equality is preserved exactly.
//
// cost:
// - Pure queries and logit adjustments (`GenerateLogits`, `GetHighestLogitToken`,
//   `GetTokenLogit`, `IsTokenValidNext`) do not change `helpers.cost` or
//   `steps`, so `helpers.cost <= steps` is unchanged.
// - The charged helper branches `OpenConstrainedSpan`, `CloseConstrainedSpan`,
//   and `ConstrainedStep` each bump `helpers.cost` by 1 internally, and in the
//   same branch we increment `steps` by 1 before any subsequent iteration or
//   return. In the raw `ChooseNextToken` branch we manually do
//   `helpers.cost := helpers.cost + 1` and also increment `steps` by 1. If a
//   branch breaks after EOS, it does so after the matching `steps` increment,
//   so even on control-flow exit the accounting inequality still holds.
//
// progress:
// - The invariant is `|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + 2 * steps`. Pure query
//   operations do not change either side. In every charged branch we first
//   account for one more step and then perform at most one helper action that
//   changes `generated`.
// - Outside/raw sampling and constrained append branches add at most one token
//   to `generated`, so after `steps := steps + 1` the right-hand side grows by
//   2 while the left-hand side grows by at most 1. The EOS sub-branches add
//   zero tokens and therefore also preserve the bound.
// - `OpenConstrainedSpan` and `CloseConstrainedSpan` are the only delimiter
//   branches; each may enlarge `generated`, but by design we charge them under
//   the coarser two-tokens-per-step bound. Thus after incrementing `steps` by 1,
//   any growth caused by opening or closing remains within the new allowance.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;
helpers.cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + 2 * steps
  invariant cost == 0
  invariant helpers.cost <= steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if insideConstrainedOut {
    if parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) {
      var gClose, inClose, curClose := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
      generated := gClose;
